{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/doubleSharp","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A double sharp accidental."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"doubleSharp"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue\/doublesharp"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"MXLAccidentalValue.doubleSharp","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"doubleSharp"}],"symbolKind":"case","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL18MXLAccidentalValueO11doubleSharpyA2CmF"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The accidental-value type represents notated accidentals supported by MusicXML. In the MusicXML 2.0 DTD this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"was a string with values that could be included. The XSD strengthens the data typing to an enumerated list."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The quarter- and three-quarters- accidentals are Tartini-style quarter-tone accidentals. The -down and -up"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals are quarter-tone accidentals that include arrows pointing down or up. The slash- accidentals are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"used in Turkish classical music. The numbered sharp and flat accidentals are superscripted versions of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidental signs, used in Turkish folk music. The sori and koron accidentals are microtonal sharp and flat"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accidentals used in Iranian and Persian music. The other accidental covers accidentals other than those listed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"here. It is usually used in combination with the smufl attribute to specify a particular SMuFL accidental. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute may be used with any accidental value to help specify the appearance of symbols that share the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same MusicXML semantics."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLAccidentalValue","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLAccidentalValue"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLAccidentalValue/doubleSharp":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A double sharp accidental.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlaccidentalvalue\/doublesharp","title":"MXLAccidentalValue.doubleSharp","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLAccidentalValue\/doubleSharp","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"doubleSharp","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"}}}